Hello 0-day maintainers,

I would like to request the inclusion of the Pengutronix 0-day git tree
into the regular testing of the 0-day builder.

The intended usage model of this tree is that all Pengutronix
developers have a canonical location for patches they would like to
feed into the 0-day builder before they hit the public mailing lists.
So it would be nice if all changed branches in that repo could be built
by the robot.

I am the primary contact for any issues regarding this tree, but as a
fallback a mail to kernel(a)pengutronix.de will reach the right people.

The tree can be fetched via git from
	git://git.pengutronix.de/linux-0-day
or via https from
	https://git.pengutronix.de/git/linux-0-day

Thanks,
Lucas

